        readonly title: "Ground Penetrating Radar in Dense Urban Corridors: Mitigating Utility Strikes";
        readonly category: "Case Study";
        readonly publishDate: "2026-09-12";
        readonly summary: "Best practices for multi-frequency electromagnetic locating and GPR radargrams prior to deep piling for elevated viaducts.";
        readonly content: "## Eliminating the Risk of Utility Strikes\n\nDeep bored piling in city centers presents severe risks to buried gas lines, fiber optic backbones, and high-voltage transmission cables. A single utility strike can trigger massive blackouts, gas leaks, and multi-week project delays.\n\nGeospatial Works provides comprehensive Subsurface Utility Engineering (SUE) Quality Level B and A services, utilizing shielded ground penetrating radar arrays and electromagnetic induction to produce 3D underground collision maps.";
